<%#
  reCAPTCHA widget.

  Expects `captcha` = { siteKey, mode }. Renders nothing when no site key is
  configured, so a form never shows a broken widget.

  Two modes, both reCAPTCHA v2:

    checkbox  - the familiar "I'm not a robot" box. Works with a standard v2 key.
    invisible - no box at all. The challenge appears only when Google is unsure,
                so a normal visitor sees nothing. Needs a key registered as
                "reCAPTCHA v2 - Invisible" in the Google admin console.

  No data-callback here. The widget is rendered explicitly by main.js, which
  passes the callback in the render options - a callback named in the markup
  would have to be a global, and it could not tell one form's widget from
  another's on a page that carries two.
%>
<% if (captcha && captcha.siteKey) { %>
  <% if (captcha.mode === 'invisible') { %>
    <div class="recaptcha-wrap">
      <div class="g-recaptcha"
           data-sitekey="<%= captcha.siteKey %>"
           data-size="invisible"
           data-badge="bottomright"></div>
      <p class="form-hint" style="text-align:center">
        Protected by reCAPTCHA. No action needed — verification is automatic.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% } else { %>
    <div class="recaptcha-wrap">
      <div class="g-recaptcha" data-sitekey="<%= captcha.siteKey %>"></div>
    </div>
  <% } %>
<% } %>
